SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loughcrew]; The tombs sit on top of hills (they keep watch from the hilltops) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loughcrew]; The hills with the tombs are the highest point in Meath [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loughcrew]; The tombs are ancient (4th millennium BC) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loughcrew]; Some (not all) of the tombs are decorated with megalithic art [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loughcrew]; The megalithic art at Loughcrew is rare [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loughcrew]; The tombs are estimated to date from about 3300 BC [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loughcrew]"}]'::jsonb),
